# Gitignored files COPIED (not symlinked) into each Orca worktree, so every
# worktree owns a private copy it can edit without touching the primary.
# See orca.yaml for the symlinked (shared) dependency dirs.

# App config. Copied — NOT shared — precisely so each worktree can point at its
# own database/queue and avoid the collisions below. After a worktree is
# created, edit its .env:
#   DB_DATABASE=seatplus_<worktree>   # give each worktree its own pgsql DB
#                                     # (createdb it first) so parallel
#                                     # migrate:fresh runs don't wipe each other
#   REDIS_PREFIX=<worktree>:          # isolate cache keys on the shared Redis
#   REDIS_DB / REDIS_QUEUE            # separate Horizon queues if running >1
.env

# composer-merge path-repo overrides for the seatplus/* checkouts (generated by
# `composer run local:on`). Copied so a worktree keeps resolving seatplus/* locally.
#
# The urls are ABSOLUTE and anchored on the primary checkout's workspace, so this
# copy is correct as-is inside a worktree at any path — including Orca's
# ~/orca/workspaces/<project>/<slug>, which lives outside the workspace dir. That
# is why absolute matters: a relative `../web` would point at a nonexistent path
# there, and composer treats a missing path repo as a WARNING, silently falling
# back to Packagist — your package edits would appear to do nothing.
#
# Regenerate with `composer run local:on` if the workspace moves; it is safe to run
# from inside a worktree (it re-derives the same primary anchor via
# `git rev-parse --git-common-dir`, so it reproduces an identical file).
composer.local.json

# ── Test-DB isolation (read before running suites in parallel) ────────────────
# Each Postgres-using package pins its OWN test DB via phpunit.xml force="true":
# auth -> laravel_auth, eveapi -> laravel_eveapi, web -> laravel_web
# (esi-client / esi-schema use no DB). So DIFFERENT packages' suites run in
# parallel safely. The force pin also means test runs ignore the per-worktree
# DB_DATABASE set in .env above — that value is for running the actual app, not
# the tests. createdb the per-package test DBs once on the host Postgres.
# Remaining limit: two worktrees of the SAME package share that package's test
# DB — don't run `composer run test` for the same package in two worktrees at
# once. Browser tests are unaffected — they only run in the "Browser (vs core)"
# CI job, not locally.
